cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SegmentART: assisted image annotation with SAM 2 and semantic grouping"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Faci
    given-names: Adam
  - family-names: Maronet
    given-names: Léa
abstract: >-
  SegmentART is an image annotation tool that combines manual prompts (box,
  positive and negative points) with automatic segmentation by SAM 2, then
  groups the resulting objects semantically and describes them in a structured,
  Visual Genome style format. It is designed to reduce the time and the number
  of interactions required for dense annotation, and it records fine grained
  interaction telemetry so that annotation strategies can be compared.
keywords:
  - image annotation
  - instance segmentation
  - SAM 2
  - interactive segmentation
  - scene graph
  - digital humanities
  - cultural heritage
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-07"
